Original commit body from 3cd76605c181c92fda2a8978bcb5d9e14ed40301:

build_opener() reads the *_proxy variables (its default ProxyHandler
calls getproxies()), so it is rowed env_read and auto-derives a
host_secret source. That source tainted the returned OpenerDirector, and
taint carries a sink's receiver, so every opener.open(url) read violated
on host_secret -> network with no secret in any argument, while
urlopen(url), which does the same read, read clean.

Owner ruling (2026-10-04, re-confirmed 2026-10-20): opener sends stay
clean. A handle constructor's own configuration read is not data sent
through the handle (ADR-0049 Ruling 4).

- io_primitives rows may declare `returns_handle: true`, inbound
  boundaries only, validated at load. The crossing stays classified;
  the derived TaintSource carries return_tainted=False.
- find_source_callers mints nothing for a caller-seeded source that
  taints neither its return nor an argument (_taints_a_value). A
  callee-seeded source names an entry point and always mints.
- Marked: urllib.request ProxyHandler, build_opener, URLopener,
  FancyURLopener, xml.dom.getDOMImplementation. getproxies* return the
  mapping and keep minting.
- ADR-0049 records the ruling and states this is not a deferred
  crossing, so Ruling 2's opacity gate does not apply. WI-dibit's pin
  test now asserts the ruled behaviour.

Ported from the patit half of parked draft 206e733d13 (its WI-tumol half
landed as e1b4e10b7c). INV-komoj's return lift also reads
return_tainted, so a helper returning build_opener() lifts nothing;
tested, with a control that a helper returning os.environ still lifts.

Measured (verify-claims, host_secret -> network): build_opener().open
and build_opener(ProxyHandler()).open with no secret go violated ->
confirmed; a secret sent as data stays violated with os.environ as its
only source; getproxies() -> ProxyHandler(p) stays violated through
getproxies. Corpus A/B, dev vs branch, 7 claims, every corpus repo
calling one of the five constructors (pytorch tools/linter, django,
superset): 5 flows removed, 0 added, 0 verdicts moved. All five removed
flows are rooted in build_opener / ProxyHandler, none carries a secret.

